# Expectation record for 12_preprocessor/005_variadic_macros.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 005_variadic_macros
area               = 12_preprocessor
description        = Variadic macros: forwarding a variadic list at three arities, forwarding it through a second variadic macro, the empty variadic list reached by two strictly conforming routes, and stringizing an empty, a single-token and a multi-token list
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined and no unspecified behaviour. Every arithmetic operand is a small
int constant and the largest value computed is 18, so no signed overflow is reachable. No shift
operator appears. There is no cast, no union and no pointer arithmetic beyond indexing a string
literal up to and including its terminator, so no aliasing rule and no bound is stressed. No object is
read before it is written. No object is modified twice between sequence points. No call receives a
side-effecting argument.

Every variadic macro invocation is strictly conforming. C11 6.10.3p4 requires an invocation of a
macro whose parameter list ends in an ellipsis to supply more arguments than there are parameters, so
every invocation of the two forwarding macros supplies at least one variadic argument. The empty
variadic list is reached only through spellings that satisfy that rule: a bare `#define M(...)`
invoked as `M()`, which supplies one empty argument, and the stringize operator applied to an empty
list, whose result C11 6.10.3.2p2 fixes as the empty string.

Stringizing is deterministic rather than incidental. 6.10.3.2p2 deletes white space before the first
token and after the last and collapses each remaining run to a single space, so the two-token list
stringizes to the same text under every conforming implementation.

ARITY OF THE STRINGIZING MACRO. The stringizing macro is itself declared variadic, and that is a
correctness requirement rather than a stylistic choice. A one-parameter stringizing macro handed a
comma-separated list is an arity error, not a comparison: measured on the same list this program
stringizes, gcc 13.4.0 reports `passed 2 arguments, but takes just 1` and clang 20.1.8 reports "too
many arguments provided to function-like macro invocation". Declaring it variadic is what lets one
macro legally receive an empty list, a single token and several tokens, which is precisely the
three-way coverage the golden record asserts. Reducing it to a single named parameter would convert
three live assertions into a compile failure owned by this test rather than by either compiler.

DETERMINISM. Every printed value is an int printed with %d or a string constant written in this
source, so nothing target-varying, address-derived, time-derived, random or locale-dependent can
reach stdout. No plain char value is printed: char signedness was measured as signed on x86_64 and
i686 and unsigned on aarch64 and riscv64, so a plain-char value would diverge for a reason that is
not a defect. No raw type width is printed: sizeof(long) and sizeof(void *) were measured as 4 on
i686 and 8 on the other three targets. Iteration order is fixed by literal bounds. main returns 0,
inside the 0-125 range the suite requires so that no exit status is truncated.

HERMETICITY. Every input is a literal in this source. Nothing is opened, nothing is read from the
environment, the command line, the clock or the file system, and no storage is allocated, so a cell
is reproducible from this source and this record alone.

GATE. The default warning gate applies unmodified and no `ub_audit_flags` key appears:
-Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror. The program was verified
clean under that gate with all four reference drivers and with the alternate reference compiler, and
it builds and runs clean under -fsanitize=undefined,address -fno-sanitize-recover=all. Both gates are
reference-compiler-only and are never applied to bcc, so requirement 3's shared-flag discipline is
untouched.

NO HEADER IS INCLUDED and printf is declared by hand as `int printf(const char *, ...);`. bcc bundles
only freestanding headers and ships no standard I/O header, so naming one would fail on the bcc side
of oracle (a) while succeeding on the reference side -- a spurious divergence caused by the test
rather than by a compiler.

NOT EVEN <stdarg.h> IS INCLUDED, which in a program about variadic macros is worth stating rather
than leaving to inference. The corpus sanctions exactly two header exceptions and this program is
neither of them: every program in area 07_variadics may include <stdarg.h> and nothing else, and
12_preprocessor/003_bundled_header_inclusion.c may include the nine required bundled headers. Nor
does this program need one. What is under test here is the preprocessor's expansion of a variadic
macro, and that expansion is complete before any runtime argument-retrieval machinery could be
reached; every helper the expansions call is ordinary fixed-arity C, so a divergence can only have
come from the expansion itself. The runtime va_list path is exercised in area 07 instead, where a
defect in it cannot be mistaken for a preprocessor defect. A maintainer who added the header would
widen this program's failure surface without widening what it tests.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
THREE SPELLINGS ARE EXCLUDED, EACH NARROWLY AND EACH FOR A STATED REASON. No target, no optimization
level and no oracle is narrowed, and no expected-divergence marker is attached.

THE GNU COMMA SWALLOW, `, ##__VA_ARGS__`, IS EXCLUDED. An earlier form of this program used it to
reach the zero-argument case. Pasting a comma with __VA_ARGS__ has no meaning in C11 -- it is a GNU
extension -- and the alternate reference compiler this suite may legitimately select as its oracle
rejects it outright under the audit gate this area declares: seven -Wgnu-zero-variadic-macro-arguments
errors, measured with clang 20.1.8. A construct that cannot survive the audit gate of a compiler that
may serve as the oracle cannot be the subject of a comparison, because the failure would be the
test's rather than the compiler's. Per constraint C3 the exclusion is stated rather than left silent,
and it is narrow: the zero-variadic-argument case, which is the property that spelling existed to
reach, is still exercised twice by strictly conforming means. The extension belongs with the other GCC
extensions in area 08, whose programs declare a gate suited to non-standard constructs.

THE C2X OPTIONAL-COMMA VARIADIC OPERATOR IS EXCLUDED because no repository document enumerates support
for it, so a compile failure arising from it would be attributable to this test rather than to the
compiler under test.

AN EXPLICIT EMPTY TRAILING MACRO ARGUMENT IS EXCLUDED because the reference compiler itself rejects
that spelling with a syntax error, so it could not form the basis of a comparison between two
compilers in the first place.

WIDTH NORMALIZATION. Every printed value is an int or a string constant written in this source, so no
target-varying width and no plain-char signedness can influence a byte of stdout.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
all_variadic_one=ok
all_variadic_two=7
all_variadic_three=3 4
named_plus_one=11
named_plus_two=5 6
nested_named_plus_one=13
nested_all_variadic_one=ok
nested_all_variadic_three=8 9
bare_noarg_macro=3
bare_noarg_add=0
va_str_empty_len=0
va_str_list=a, b
va_str_single=alpha
fixed_arity_one=5
fixed_arity_two=11
fixed_arity_three=18
END
